---
title: Egg Fried Rice
course: Side Dish
cuisine: Chinese
image: https://saracooking.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/06-Egg-Fried-Rice.png
---

== Sauce Option 1 ==

> This makes much more sauce than you need, so adjust accordingly.

Combine @soy sauce{1/3%cup}, @oyster sauce{1/3%cup}, @mirin{1/3 cup}, @seasame oil{1/4%cup}, and @black pepper{1%tbsp}.

== Sauce Option 2==

Combine @garlic{3%cloves}(minced), @ginger{1%tsp}(grated), @sweet soy sauce{1%tbsp}, @dark soy sauce{1%tbsp}, and @seasame oil{1%tbsp}.

== Frying ==

Heat up @peanut oil{1%tbsp} in a #wok on medium-low heat.

Add @garlic{5%cloves}(minced), @shallots{2}(diced), and @spring onions{3}(diced, the whites only). Stir fry until they have some color. Add @?frozen veggies{1%bag} when the shallots are starting to become translucent.

Add @eggs{3} and stir fry until cooked. They should look like scrambled eggs.

Add @rice{3%cups}(leftover long grain rice, like Jasmine. You need to make this the night before and store in tupperware) and mix, ensuring the rice is not clumped up.

Add @pepper{1%tbsp} and @MSG{1%tbsp} and mix.

Add your chosen sauce mixture and mix.

Add the greens of the spring onions from before (diced) as garnish and serve immediately.